{"Multi-override logic: `find` returns first truthy value, causing incorrect blocking when slot is outside one override but inside another. If a user has multiple date overrides on the same day, and the slot is outside the first override but inside the second, `find` will return the first override and the slot will be incorrectly marked unavailable. The logic needs to check all overrides for the day and only block if the slot is outside ALL of them.": 0.8742263913154602, "Working hours check logic is inverted \u2014 slots inside working hours are incorrectly blocked. The condition returns true when the slot is outside the working hour window, but if any working hour entry does NOT contain the slot, the slot is marked unavailable even if another working hour entry does contain it. Should use `.every()` instead of `.find()`, or invert the condition.": 0.8756031394004822, "`checkIfIsAvailable` in the `selectedSlots` path does not receive `dateOverrides` or `workingHours`, meaning for events with reserved/selected slots, the new date-override and working-hours logic is completely bypassed.": 0.5150527954101562, "Active override filter uses UTC start time but `startOfInviteeDay` is in invitee timezone \u2014 cross-midnight overrides may be missed. When the invitee is in a timezone significantly ahead of UTC, the UTC representation of the override start may fall outside the invitee's day window even though the override is valid for that day.": 0.2600424587726593, "Spreading schedule into checkIfIsAvailable passes fields inconsistently across call sites. The `availabilityCheckProps` object omits `dateOverrides` and `workingHours`, relying on spreads at individual call sites to supply them. The `dateOverrides` type also lacks `timeZone` and `userId` fields that are present on the actual objects being spread, creating a silent type mismatch.": 0.6876850724220276}